        "text": "Answers\n1.I The threads and processes are coordinated by the operating system kernel.\n2.I Python's GIL is a locking mechanism used by Python to allow only one thread to\nexecute at a time.\n3.I Daemon threads are used when it is not an issue for a thread to be terminated once\nits main thread terminates.\n4.I The Pool object keeps only the active processes in memory, so it is a better choice.\n5.I Futures are like a callback mechanism that is used to process the result coming from\nasync/await calls.\n6.I An event loop object keeps track of tasks and handles the flow of control\nbetween them.\n7.I We can write an asynchronous coroutine by starting with async def .",
